# No em dashes / plain writing

## Hard rules

- Do **not** use the em dash character (`—`, U+2014) in user-facing copy, commits, docs, product text, UI strings, or chat replies.
- Prefer a normal hyphen (`-`), a colon (`:`), a comma, or a new sentence.
- Avoid en dashes (`–`) in marketing/UI copy; use `-` for ranges (e.g. `$1.5k-$2.5k`, `15-25%`).
- Keep prose plain and direct. No padded “AI blog” tone.

## Examples

```text
Bad:  Discovery call — filled example
Good: Discovery call: filled example

Bad:  soft — before Ramadan
Good: soft, before Ramadan

Bad:  01 — Discovery call
Good: 01 - Discovery call
```

## Scope

Applies to portfolio site copy, digital product templates, admin UI strings, README/docs you edit, commit messages, and assistant replies in this repo.
